    "explanation": "This is a no-show charge of 5.00 SGD on trip TRP-05070, and the rider filed to get it back. The decision turns on POL-NS-23 (the driver's contact obligation), which requires the driver, before cancelling for no-show, to have BOTH placed at least one in-app call AND sent at least one in-app chat message to the rider, both before trip_record.cancelled_at (16:13:40). The call limb is met: two in-app calls were placed by the driver, at 16:09:30 (rang 25 s) and 16:11:50 (rang 20 s), both unanswered, both before cancellation. The message limb is not met. The only message on the chat log before 16:13:40 is 'Your driver has arrived.' (16:07:29), and its sender field is SYSTEM — a platform notification, not a message sent by the driver. The driver's own chat message, 'I cancel already, you never come down', was sent at 16:13:55, fifteen seconds AFTER he cancelled at 16:13:40, so it cannot satisfy the 'before cancelled_at' requirement either. The trip record's own derived contact check agrees: message_count 0, obligation_met false. Because one limb of POL-NS-23 is missing, the clause voids the fee — the 5.00 SGD cancellation fee charged to the rider is refunded in full, with no driver compensation. On the driver's side, I accept that POL-NS-21's precondition to cancel was satisfied: the driver marked arrival at 16:07:25, the 300 s free wait expired at 16:12:25, and he cancelled at 16:13:40, 375 s after arrival; the GPS trace corroborates arrival (nearest fix 2.16 m from the pickup at 16:07:50, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, within the 25 m accuracy filter), and the vehicle was stationary throughout. But POL-NS-21 only permits the driver to cancel; it is a precondition, not a substitute for POL-NS-23's contact obligation, so it does not save the fee. I also accept the ledger facts (single 5.00 SGD cancellation-fee line, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0) and that the fee amount matches POL-NS-22's 5.00 SGD schedule — which is why no POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral arises. The driver's argument that the automated arrival notification stands in for his own message is rejected: POL-NS-23 requires a message sent by the driver, and a SYSTEM notification is not one. POL-NS-24 gives no refund here because the driver did arrive and did attempt contact. POL-NS-25 produces no referral: the named counter rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is absent from the profile, and in any event the fee does not stand. No fraud flag is carried by either profile, and the contested 5.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so under POL-NS-26 this ruling is final. The 5.00 SGD figure is the fee_charged_sgd / policy_fee_sgd of 5.00 read from the fare breakdown, and it is the whole amount contested.",
    "confidence_basis": null
